en for autism and ADHD]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/133468829.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/science/meet-edward-kang-the-17-year-old-new-jersey-student-who-used-retinal-images-to-train-ai-for-autism-and-adhd-screening-his-project-won-a-175000-science-prize/articleshow/133468829.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/science/meet-edward-kang-the-17-year-old-new-jersey-student-who-used-retinal-images-to-train-ai-for-autism-and-adhd-screening-his-project-won-a-175000-science-prize/articleshow/133468829.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-08-25T01:00:00+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI Science Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-133469010,imgsize-146820.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[In 1908, an Indiana widow began 20-year fight over 120 acres; part of land later became protected]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/133463363.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[Drusilla Carr, an unschooled Indiana widow, spent more than two decades defending her claim to 120 acres along Lake Michigan. As Gary expanded and the lakeshore became valuable, she fought repeated legal battles against attempts to acquire the land. Decades after her death, part of her former property was included in a 212-acre donation that became protected land within Indiana Dunes National Lakeshore.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/in-1908-an-unschooled-indiana-widow-began-a-20-year-fight-to-defend-120-acres-of-lake-michigan-dunes-from-a-steel-giant-72-years-later-212-acres-including-part-of-her-tract-joined-indiana-dunes-to-remain-open-space-forever/articleshow/133463363.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/in-1908-an-unschooled-indiana-widow-began-a-20-year-fight-to-defend-120-acres-of-lake-michigan-dunes-from-a-steel-giant-72-years-later-212-acres-including-part-of-her-tract-joined-indiana-dunes-to-remain-open-space-forever/articleshow/133463363.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-08-24T23:55:00+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-133466044,imgsize-78016.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Colorado land sold for 30 cents an acre later helped create a vast national park]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/133463849.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/in-1862-heirs-sold-colorados-baca-land-for-30-cents-an-acre-140-years-later-its-97000-acre-ranch-sold-for-31-28-million-and-helped-create-a-national-park-nearly-four-times-the-monuments-original-size/articleshow/133463849.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/in-1862-heirs-sold-colorados-baca-land-for-30-cents-an-acre-140-years-later-its-97000-acre-ranch-sold-for-31-28-million-and-helped-create-a-national-park-nearly-four-times-the-monuments-original-size/articleshow/133463849.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-08-24T22:47:30+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-133464112,imgsize-115431.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Michigan couple bought 160-year-old farmhouse for $26K, spent $320K rebuilding it without experience]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/133473372.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[A Michigan couple bought an abandoned 160-year-old farmhouse for $26,000 and spent nearly $320,000 bringing it back to life. Samantha and Sean Kilgore tackled the massive restoration without professional renovation experience, transforming everything from the foundation to the kitchen. Their journey turned a neglected property into a beautiful home while preserving its history and character.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/real-estate/in-2018-a-young-michigan-couple-bought-an-abandoned-160-year-old-farmhouse-for-26000-with-no-renovation-experience-they-spent-about-320000-rebuilding-it/articleshow/133473372.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/real-estate/in-2018-a-young-michigan-couple-bought-an-abandoned-160-year-old-farmhouse-for-26000-with-no-renovation-experience-they-spent-about-320000-rebuilding-it/articleshow/133473372.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-08-24T22:15:24+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI Real Estate Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-133473588,imgsize-119933.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[12 people arrested in connection with UK A66 crash that killed 7, including 2 police officers]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/133473276.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/uk/12-people-arrested-in-connection-with-uk-a66-crash-that-killed-7-including-2-police-officers/articleshow/133473276.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/uk/12-people-arrested-in-connection-with-uk-a66-crash-that-killed-7-including-2-police-officers/articleshow/133473276.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-08-24T21:56:46+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-133473336,imgsize-938392.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Blind Egyptian entrepreneur builds AI app to help users experience the world through audio]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/133463516.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/rest-of-world/a-blind-egyptian-entrepreneur-built-an-ai-app-that-describes-the-world-through-audio-helping-visually-impaired-users-experience-wildlife-objects-and-surrounding-scenes-through-their-phones/articleshow/133463516.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/rest-of-world/a-blind-egyptian-entrepreneur-built-an-ai-app-that-describes-the-world-through-audio-helping-visually-impaired-users-experience-wildlife-objects-and-surrounding-scenes-through-their-phones/articleshow/133463516.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-08-24T21:47:10+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-133463677,imgsize-154363.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA['I was living paycheck to paychek': Woman says coming back to India from UK after 4 years not happiest decision but right one for nervous system]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/133472486.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/uk/i-was-living-paycheck-to-paychek-woman-says-coming-back-to-india-from-uk-after-4-years-not-happiest-decision-but-right-one-for-nervous-system/articleshow/133472486.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/uk/i-was-living-paycheck-to-paychek-woman-says-coming-back-to-india-from-uk-after-4-years-not-happiest-decision-but-right-one-for-nervous-system/articleshow/133472486.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-08-24T21:17:18+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-133472600,imgsize-109856.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Researchers develop 3D-printed replacements for missing pottery parts, embed sensors in them]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/133459889.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[Researchers at Koc University have developed a method that uses photogrammetry, 3D printing and embedded sensors to repair damaged ancient pottery. The customised 3D-printed sections can replace missing parts while monitoring temperature, humidity, pH and physical stress. Tested on maritime amphorae from Türkiye and Italy, the approach could help conservators track changes and support long-term preservation.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/science/researchers-developed-custom-3d-printed-replacements-for-missing-sections-of-ancient-pottery-and-embedded-sensors-inside-them-allowing-conservators-to-monitor-temperature-strain-and-environmental-damage/articleshow/133459889.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/science/researchers-developed-custom-3d-printed-replacements-for-missing-sections-of-ancient-pottery-and-embedded-sensors-inside-them-allowing-conservators-to-monitor-temperature-strain-and-environmental-damage/articleshow/133459889.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-08-24T20:50:13+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI Science Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-133463128,imgsize-106315.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[A black hole keeps tearing pieces off the same star, yet the star survives and comes back again]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/133463351.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[Astronomers have made fascinating observations of stars that are caught in a gravitational dance with supermassive black holes. As these stars approach, they lose material in a series of light bursts that fade over time. New research indicates that the stars' rapid initial spin is key to this phenomenon, as it limits excessive rotation during subsequent encounters with the black holes.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/science/some-stars-repeatedly-skim-past-supermassive-black-holes-lose-material-and-survive-scientists-now-think-their-unusually-rapid-spin-explains-why-each-returning-flare-becomes-progressively-dimmer/articleshow/133463351.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/science/some-stars-repeatedly-skim-past-supermassive-black-holes-lose-material-and-survive-scientists-now-think-their-unusually-rapid-spin-explains-why-each-returning-flare-becomes-progressively-dimmer/articleshow/133463351.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-08-24T20:50:03+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI Science Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-133463501,imgsize-323888.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Quote of the Day by Benjamin Franklin: "Well done is better than well said"]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/133471191.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/rest-of-world/quote-of-the-day-by-benjamin-franklin-well-done-is-better-than-well-said/articleshow/133471191.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/rest-of-world/quote-of-the-day-by-benjamin-franklin-well-done-is-better-than-well-said/articleshow/133471191.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-08-24T20:19:08+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-133471378,imgsize-524490.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Albany Police Department issues BOLO for a man who picked $30 from the floor while shopping at Walmart; faces backlash, says no charges will be filed]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/133470460.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/albany-police-department-issues-bolo-for-a-man-who-picked-30-from-the-floor-while-shopping-at-walmart-faces-backlash-says-no-charges-will-be-filed/articleshow/133470460.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/albany-police-department-issues-bolo-for-a-man-who-picked-30-from-the-floor-while-shopping-at-walmart-faces-backlash-says-no-charges-will-be-filed/articleshow/133470460.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-08-24T19:47:39+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-133470529,imgsize-124720.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Arthur creator Marc Brown sells Martha’s Vineyard home for $6.4 million after 37 years]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/133461143.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[Marc Brown, the creator of Arthur, along with his wife, has sold their beloved Martha's Vineyard estate for a substantial $6.4 million. This historic property, meticulously restored over thirty-seven years, was a sanctuary for Brown's creativity, where he penned half the Arthur books. With this sale, they conclude a significant chapter in their lives and have already acquired a new home in New York's Hudson Valley, ready for restoration.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/in-1988-arthur-creator-marc-brown-bought-a-marthas-vineyard-estate-for-700000-after-37-years-and-writing-half-the-books-there-he-sold-it-for-6-4-million/articleshow/133461143.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/in-1988-arthur-creator-marc-brown-bought-a-marthas-vineyard-estate-for-700000-after-37-years-and-writing-half-the-books-there-he-sold-it-for-6-4-million/articleshow/133461143.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-08-24T19:45:00+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-133461309,imgsize-235848.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[In 1998, Costa Rica spread 12,000 tonnes of orange waste; 16 years later, forest biomass rose 176%]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/133466780.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[In 1998, about 12,000 metric tonnes of orange peels and pulp were spread over a degraded pasture in Costa Rica as part of an unusual forest restoration experiment. Sixteen years later, researchers found that the site had developed into a dense forest, with richer soil, greater tree diversity and a 176% increase in aboveground biomass.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/rest-of-world/in-1998-costa-rica-spread-12000-tonnes-of-orange-waste-over-degraded-pasture-16-years-later-tree-diversity-had-tripled-and-forest-biomass-was-176-higher/articleshow/133466780.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/rest-of-world/in-1998-costa-rica-spread-12000-tonnes-of-orange-waste-over-degraded-pasture-16-years-later-tree-diversity-had-tripled-and-forest-biomass-was-176-higher/articleshow/133466780.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-08-24T19:20:28+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-133468565,imgsize-312188.cms"/></item></channel></rss>